<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐερύω</span></b> , i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀϝ-ϝερύω,</span>
		
			Ep.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀν-ϝερύω,</span>
		=
		
			Att.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναρρύω</span>: aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐέρῠσα</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>draw back</i> or <i>backwards,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς [στήλας] οἵ γ᾽ αὐέρυον</span>
			<i>pulled</i> them <i>backwards,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.261
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόξον αὐερύοντα παρ᾽ ὦμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.325
				</span></i>
			: mostly abs., in sacrifice, <i>draw</i> the victim's head
				<i>back,</i> so as to cut its throat, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐέρυσαν μὲν πρῶτα καὶ ἔσφαξαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.459
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				13.81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.241
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.96
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Eryc.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of leeches,
				<i>suck,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.603
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
